# Two harness generations, both kept because the worklog's identity numbers come from the first.
#
# Part 1 is the run of 2026-11-08 on primerose (A100 80GB PCIe). Its harness ignored every CUDA
# return value, so "mismatches 0" there means the comparison agreed *if* the copy and the launch
# that produced its inputs happened at all — which is #26's finding.
# Part 2 is the checked harness (CUDA_CHECK around every call), recorded by ./bit-identity.sh,
# which prints the exit code of each run. Re-run it on a device for the identity rows; that is
# the one thing this revision does not have.

# --- Part 1: primerose, A100 80GB PCIe, driver 580.178.04, unchecked harness ---------------
# $ nvcc -std=c++17 -arch=sm_80 -o eq bit-identity.cu && ./eq   (CUDA 12.6, A100 80GB PCIe, driver 580.178.04)
# This revision of the program also echoed the last CUDA error into each line: the checked
# harness has no such field, because a failure now ends the run instead of being printed.
f32: 67109120 pairs (16 special^2 + 67108864 random), mismatches 0, cuda no error
f64: 67109120 pairs (16 special^2 + 67108864 random), mismatches 0, cuda no error
total mismatches 0
# exit 0

# --- Part 2: evo2 (Ryzen AI MAX+ 395, no NVIDIA device, no driver), checked harness ---------
# $ ./bit-identity.sh    (CUDA 12.6 Build cuda_12.6.r12.6/compiler.35059454_0)
# The failures below are the first CUDA call, cudaMalloc, so this records the failure paths and
# not the identity. Note what the last block does: with the return values ignored, the same run
# prints `mismatches 0` and exits 0 having compared nothing.
# no NVIDIA device: nvidia-smi gives no answer
# nvcc --version | tail -1: Build cuda_12.6.r12.6/compiler.35059454_0
# exit 0  (nvcc -std=c++17 -arch=sm_80 -o bit-identity bit-identity.cu)

## same values, checked
$ ./bit-identity 
FAILED /home/shinaoka/work/cuda-26/docs/worklogs/evidence/2026-11-08-nan-extrema-select/bit-identity.cu:45 cudaMalloc(&da, bytes) -> CUDA driver version is insufficient for CUDA runtime version
mode checked, 67108864 random pairs per type, copy as allocated
# exit 2

## copy from a null host pointer, checked
$ ./bit-identity --copy-fails
FAILED /home/shinaoka/work/cuda-26/docs/worklogs/evidence/2026-11-08-nan-extrema-select/bit-identity.cu:45 cudaMalloc(&da, bytes) -> CUDA driver version is insufficient for CUDA runtime version
mode checked, 67108864 random pairs per type, copy from a null pointer
# exit 2

## allocation the device cannot satisfy (160 GB on an 80 GB card), checked
$ ./bit-identity --n 40000000000
FAILED /home/shinaoka/work/cuda-26/docs/worklogs/evidence/2026-11-08-nan-extrema-select/bit-identity.cu:45 cudaMalloc(&da, bytes) -> CUDA driver version is insufficient for CUDA runtime version
mode checked, 40000000000 random pairs per type, copy as allocated
# exit 2

## copy from a null host pointer, every return value ignored (the pre-fix harness)
$ ./bit-identity --legacy --copy-fails
mode legacy (every CUDA return value ignored), 67108864 random pairs per type, copy from a null pointer
f32: 67109120 pairs (16 special^2 + 67108864 random), mismatches 0
f64: 67109120 pairs (16 special^2 + 67108864 random), mismatches 0
total mismatches 0
# exit 0
